# Optional configuration. Fresh installations do not need a .env file.
# Copy this file only when choosing external engines or overriding defaults.
# Leave engine paths commented to use the writable managed installation home.
# Existing implicit external checkouts are preserved. Explicit paths always win.
# OPENFABRIC_MODULE_ROOT=/absolute/writable/path/openfabric-runtime

# Optional external engine paths. Examples are placeholders: use your real paths.
# ACE_STEP_DIR=/absolute/path/ACE-Step-1.5
# YUE2_DIR=/absolute/path/YuE2
# DEMUCS_DIR=/absolute/path/Demucs
# SEED_VC_DIR=/absolute/path/seed-vc
# OPENFABRIC_GPT_SOVITS_DIR=/absolute/path/gpt-sovits
# LTX_DIR=/absolute/path/ltx-2-mlx

# Set up optional engines through Settings → Setup & modules.
# Downloading model weights is explicit. Speech pretrained weights require the
# upstream setup instructions; GPT-SoVITS uses api.py on loopback port 9880.
# OPENFABRIC_GPT_SOVITS_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9880
# OPENFABRIC_SPEECH_CLONE_MOCK=1

# FFmpeg AND FFprobe must be installed. Managed tools or PATH work by default.
# FFMPEG_BIN_DIR=/absolute/path/ffmpeg/bin
# Windows native YuE may also need its CUDA toolkit DLL directory on PATH.
# CUDA_BIN_DIR=C:\Program Files\NVIDIA GPU Computing Toolkit\CUDA\your-version\bin

# MOBI import requires Calibre. The installer is linked in Settings; a typical
# macOS path is /Applications/calibre.app/Contents/MacOS/ebook-convert.
# OPENFABRIC_EBOOK_CONVERT=/absolute/path/ebook-convert

# Where songs, voices, videos, singing models, logs, and the catalog live.
# Leave unset for backend/data (logs go in its logs folder). The Data folder
# on the home page overrides OPENFABRIC_DATA_DIR after a restart. The desktop
# app sets OPENFABRIC_LOG_DIR itself, next to its data folder.
# OPENFABRIC_DATA_DIR=D:\OpenFabricStudio\data
# OPENFABRIC_LOG_DIR=D:\OpenFabricStudio\logs

# Optional internal model API ports. Useful when another local service already
# occupies OpenFabric Studio defaults. These APIs remain loopback-only.
# ACE_STEP_API_PORT=8001
# YUE2_SERVER_PORT=8080

# Optional Linux/headless settings. Leave device values blank to let each
# backend choose automatically. Setting both to different device values also
# opts into concurrent model residency; otherwise switching remains exclusive.
# UV_BIN=/absolute/path/to/uv
# CUDA_LIB_DIR=/usr/local/cuda/lib64
# ACE_STEP_DEVICE=0
# YUE2_SERVER_HOST=127.0.0.1
# YUE2_DEVICE=1

# Optional ACE-Step checkpoint folder names under ACE_STEP_DIR/checkpoints.
# Defaults are the fast turbo DiT and the 1.7B LM. On a machine with at
# least 24GB of memory, ACE-Step's higher-quality pair is the XL sft DiT
# and the 4B LM. Download them with acestep-download before pointing here.
# ACE_STEP_DIT_MODEL=acestep-v15-xl-sft
# ACE_STEP_LM_MODEL=acestep-5Hz-lm-4B
# Load a different downloaded DiT when the form asks for one (xl-base is
# the model that supports extract, lego, and complete).
# ACE_STEP_ON_DEMAND_MODEL_LOAD=true

# Optional installed MSST vocal separator for the Voice Clone RoFormer mode.
# setup_roformer.sh downloads/verifies the pinned Kimberley vocal checkpoint,
# installs its matching config and fills these values. Restart the backend.
# These examples are for manually managed matching artifacts.
# VOICE_ROFORMER_DIR=/absolute/path/to/Music-Source-Separation-Training
# VOICE_ROFORMER_MODEL_TYPE=mel_band_roformer
# VOICE_ROFORMER_CONFIG=/absolute/path/to/vocal-config.yaml
# VOICE_ROFORMER_CHECKPOINT=/absolute/path/to/vocal-model.ckpt

# Local character LoRA for silent videos and reels. Point this at the video
# engine Python (the ltx-2-mlx .venv). OpenFabric then runs its own trainer
# script, which calls that checkout's train command. No weights are downloaded.
# Leave it unset to save a dry-run job in the app. A locked still is not training.
# OPENFABRIC_VIDEO_CHARACTER_TRAINER=/absolute/path/ltx-2-mlx/.venv/bin/python
# OPENFABRIC_VIDEO_CHARACTER_TRAIN_STEPS=800
# OPENFABRIC_VIDEO_CHARACTER_TRAIN_RANK=32

# Optional local engines. Leave commented to use the managed installation home.
# Setup clones the pinned source only. It does not download model weights.
# Kokoro is preset narration (not a clone) and does not replace GPT-SoVITS.
# On a Mac, Kokoro's own hint is PYTORCH_ENABLE_MPS_FALLBACK=1.
# OPENFABRIC_KOKORO_DIR=/absolute/path/kokoro
# Chatterbox is a zero-shot clone. Original and multilingual can use mps.
# Turbo is not a Mac path and is not called.
# OPENFABRIC_CHATTERBOX_DIR=/absolute/path/chatterbox
# Wan 2.2 through mlx-video is Apple Silicon only, and only TI2V-5B.
# 14B, S2V, and Animate are not wired. Weights stay a separate explicit step.
# OPENFABRIC_WAN22_DIR=/absolute/path/mlx-video
# RVC is timbre conversion. On a Mac the packages are CPU, not GPU.
# It does not replace Seed-VC.
# OPENFABRIC_RVC_DIR=/absolute/path/rvc
